json/code
description: JSON code, JavaScript Object Notation
- >
  **JSON** (JavaScript Object Notation) is a text format for structured data. A JSON code is one
  single value — anything from a bare `42` to a deep nesting of objects and lists:
- !!<format: text/x-json> |
  {
    "name": "Julia",
    "age": 42,
    "pets": ["cat", "scorpion"],
    "address": null
  }
- >
  Every value belongs to one of two families — **structured** values that nest further values, and
  **scalar** values that nest nothing. See the subchapters below for the two families:
- *: 00-json_structured
- *: 01-json_scalar
